## 1.4 Component Registry in C++

The bridge needs to know how to instantiate any component that SynthSkin Studio can produce. Build a registry:

```cpp
class ComponentRegistry {
public:
    using ComponentFactory = std::function<std::unique_ptr<juce::Component>(const ComponentSpec&)>;
    
    void registerType(const juce::String& typeName, ComponentFactory factory);
    std::unique_ptr<juce::Component> create(const juce::String& typeName, const ComponentSpec& spec);
    
    juce::StringArray getRegisteredTypes() const;
};
```

Required built-in component types for this milestone:
- `knob` (with all material/preset variants)
- `slider` (linear, vertical, horizontal)
- `rotarySwitch` (stepped selector)
- `button` (momentary, toggle)
- `led` (round, rectangular, with animations)
- `meter` (VU, peak, RMS)
- `display` (LCD/OLED placeholder)
- `label` (with text effects)
- `section` (group container)
- `image` (custom imported asset)

Each type knows how to:
1. Construct itself from a `ComponentSpec` (the parsed XML)
2. Apply property updates at runtime (when SynthSkin sends `update_component`)
3. Bind to APVTS parameters
4. Render itself with current lighting/material settings

## 1.5 SynthSkin Studio Side: Connection Manager

In the Studio app, add a new panel/workspace area for managing live JUCE connections:

**Connection Panel UI**:
- Status indicator: Disconnected / Searching / Connected / Error
- "Scan for plugins" button - actively probes localhost ports 9876-9886
- List of detected plugins with: name, version, port, "Connect" button
- For connected plugin: name, status, last sync time, "Disconnect" button
- Error log with timestamps

**Connection logic**:
- On connect, immediately send the current design state to the plugin
- Subsequent design changes are sent as incremental updates (not full reloads)
- Heartbeat every 2 seconds to detect disconnection
- Auto-reconnect attempts with exponential backoff
- Visual indicator in the main canvas when connected (small "LIVE" badge)

## 1.6 Live Sync Behavior

When connected, every design change in SynthSkin Studio must propagate to the plugin within 100ms:

- Component property changes: send `update_component` with only the changed properties
- Component additions/deletions: send corresponding messages
- Lighting changes: send `update_lighting` (the bridge re-renders all components)
- Background changes: send `update_background`

**Conflict handling**: If the user changes a parameter value in the DAW while connected, the plugin sends `parameter_changed` to the Studio. The Studio updates its internal state but does NOT echo back (to avoid loops).

**Performance requirement**: Live sync must remain smooth even when the user rapidly drags a property slider in the Studio. Use throttling: collect updates within a 16ms window and send them as a batch.

## 1.7 The "Bake" Operation

When the user is happy with the design, they need to convert it from "live mode" to "production mode":

- "Bake to BinaryData" button in the Export workspace
- Generates the final design XML
- Generates BinaryData wrapper code that embeds the XML and all asset files
- Generates a small loader function the user adds to their `PluginEditor` constructor:

```cpp
// In PluginEditor constructor (release build):
#if !SYNTHSKIN_BRIDGE_ENABLED
    SynthSkinDesignLoader::loadFromBinaryData(
        *this, processor,
        BinaryData::design_xml,
        BinaryData::design_xmlSize
    );
#else
    bridge.startLiveMode(*this, processor);
#endif
```

The release build never runs the bridge code at all - it loads the static design from BinaryData and creates components directly. This is critical for performance and security.

